diff --git a/.github/workflows/android.yml b/.github/workflows/android.yml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..528b3de
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.github/workflows/android.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+name: android apk
+
+# The app's APKs for both ABIs. The game's code library is never built here (it is made from the
+# player's own game, on their PC or phone), so these APKs are ready to install; the player then
+# builds the library from their copy of the game (on the phone: Build on this phone; or on a PC with
+# --32bit for the armeabi-v7a APK).
+
+on:
+  push:
+  workflow_dispatch:
+
+jobs:
+  apk:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    strategy:
+      fail-fast: false
+      matrix:
+        abi: [arm64-v8a, armeabi-v7a]
+    env:
+      ANDROID_ABI: ${{ matrix.abi }}
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+
+      - uses: actions/setup-java@v4
+        with:
+          distribution: temurin
+          java-version: '17'
+
+      - name: Android SDK (NDK 27.0.12077973, platform 35)
+        run: |
+          sdkmanager --install "ndk;27.0.12077973" "platforms;android-35" "build-tools;35.0.0" >/dev/null
+
+      - name: Tools (ninja)
+        run: |
+          sudo apt-get update -qq
+          sudo apt-get install -y -qq ninja-build
+
+      - name: SDL3 (${{ matrix.abi }})
+        run: sh scripts/build_sdl3.sh
+
+      - name: APK (${{ matrix.abi }})
+        run: sh scripts/build_apk.sh
+
+      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
+        with:
+          name: mh4u-native-${{ matrix.abi }}
+          path: android/app/build/outputs/apk/**/*.apk
+          if-no-files-found: error
diff --git a/ARM32.md b/ARM32.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1d18758
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ARM32.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# The 32-bit app (armeabi-v7a)
+
+4u-native is arm64-only upstream. This branch adds a second app, built for `armeabi-v7a`: the same
+game, the same recompiled-C approach, on 32-bit phones (a Helio G25 / Redmi 9A class device).
+
+## What it changes
+
+- **The guest's C is 32-bit everywhere** (the 3DS is a 32-bit machine): the recompiler's output was
+  already portable C, so the library just compiles for `armv7a-linux-androideabi29` (`--32bit`, or
+  nothing at all on a 32-bit phone: the on-phone builder picks it from `uname`).
+- **The guest memory's reservation**: a 64-bit host reserves 4 GiB flat; a 32-bit process cannot.
+  The 32-bit build reserves the kernel's managed window only (`kManagedEnd`, 1 GiB — everything an
+  app can have mapped: FCRAM, linear heaps, VRAM, DSP RAM are all below it) plus a guard. The app
+  reserves the hole before SDL and the GPU driver map theirs (`ReserveEarlyGuestSpace`, the first
+  `Reserve()` takes it), so it succeeds even on a full 32-bit address space.
+- **Fibers**: `port/src/fiber_arm32.S` switches them (AAPCS callee-saved: r4-r11, sp, lr, d8-d15),
+  next to `fiber_arm64.S`; the same first-entry contract (r0 = the context's arg).
+- **The player's own GPU driver path** (libadrenotools, Adreno-only upstream anyway) is compiled
+  out of the 32-bit app: the system's driver is used. Everything else of the Vulkan renderer is
+  ABI-independent.
+- **The app's checks** (the game library's ELF class and machine, the crash screen's pc/lr) follow
+  the app's own ABI.
+
+## Building
+
+The APK, per ABI:
+
+```sh
+ANDROID_ABI=arm64-v8a  sh scripts/build_sdl3.sh
+ANDROID_ABI=armeabi-v7a sh scripts/build_sdl3.sh
+sh scripts/build_apk.sh                    # arm64-v8a
+ANDROID_ABI=armeabi-v7a sh scripts/build_apk.sh
+```
+
+GitHub Actions builds both APKs on every push (`.github/workflows/android.yml`).
+
+The game's code library for the 32-bit app, on a PC:
+
+```sh
+python3 tools/build_game.py --dump YOUR_UPDATE.cia [YOUR_GAME.3ds] --native --android --32bit
+```
+
+and on the phone it just picks `--32bit` on its own. The library is a 32-bit ELF, and the 32-bit
+app refuses a 64-bit one (and the other way around), so the pair cannot be mixed up.
+
+## Trying it on a 32-bit phone
+
+1. Install the `armeabi-v7a` APK (it cannot replace an installed arm64 one: Android asks to
+   uninstall first, which deletes saves — export them first).
+2. The game folder screen is the same; build the library **on this phone**, or copy one made on a
+   PC with `--32bit`.
+3. If the Vulkan device negotiation fails (the first frame's log says so), the knobs exist:
+   `MH4N_RHI_MASK` (e.g. `timeline`, `interlock`), `MH4N_NO_SHARED_IMAGES=1`, and the log line
+   `rhi: caps ...` lists what the device answered.
